      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BOAB BOY (1) earns top billing off a dominant Leonora win, where he was sent out favourite and beat The Candy Kid by just over five lengths. His Kalgoorlie third in NMW1Y grade two back reads well for this, and his 1600m record is a genuine strength. GOT LUCKY (4) is the clear danger after beating WESTERN IMPACT by three lengths at Leinster as a short odds-on favourite, with proven mile and track credentials to support the bounce. DANEA ROCK (6) brings winning form from a BM56+ at Leonora and has been honest this campaign, though the rise in grade and her broader 1600m profile temper the winning case. WESTERN IMPACT (5) has been consistent without quite breaking through, placing behind GOT LUCKY and BOAB BOY at his last two, so he profiles as the reliable exotics runner rather than the one with the sharpest winning edge. RULER ROCKET (3) has claims in the cup.",
